## Two parts soldered into one at the bench: programs/solder.cell run by
## the simulator -- the arm puts a DIP-8 in the vise and brings a
## resistor's lead to pin 3, a pincer on the turntable grips it and the
## arm goes, the turntable presents the joint to the iron station, which
## heats it and feeds its own solder; the joint freezes good, the pincer
## lets go and the resistor stays, soldered on -- each command's
## outcome a line.
## Title: The assembly cell solders
## Page: cell/live/?program=solder watch it solder, step by step, live
## Feature: Open the cell: watch a resistor soldered to a chip a command at a time, or drive it yourself, in your browser
## Run: just demo cell solder

"ce:" u_se< "Cell"
"bl:" u_se< "Blender"

"each command: ok, its end time, what happened (the joint as it froze)"
ce:r_un bl:r_ead "programs/solder.cell"
